UID:3021-1793899800-1793905200@pegs.org
SUMMARY:Whitney Stained Glass Studio | Presentation of Color and Skill
DESCRIPTION:Discover the history\, artistry\, and craftsmanship behind one of stained glass’s most celebrated traditions. \n\n\n\nJoin us for a special presentation exploring the restoration of the Tiffany Transfiguration Window and the remarkable legacy of American stained glass. Led by the General Operations Director of Whitney Stained Glass Studio\, this program will take guests behind the scenes of the restoration process while exploring the history of stained glass in our region\, the influence of Tiffany and LaFarge\, and the artistry of Tiffany Studios designer Frederick Wilson.  \n\n\n\nThrough an engaging visual presentation featuring photographs from the restoration process\, guests will gain insight into the craftsmanship\, techniques\, and dedication required to preserve these extraordinary works of art. With more than four decades of experience preserving and creating stained\, leaded\, and art glass\, Whitney Stained Glass Studio brings a unique perspective on the historical significance and artistry behind this timeless medium.  \n\n\n\nGuests will leave with a deeper understanding of the restoration process and the craftsmanship\, history\, and artistic vision that make stained glass such an enduring art form.  \n\n\n\nThis event is free and open to the public.  Free parking is available on city streets and lots throughout the walkable downtown neighborhood of Hudson\, Ohio.
URL:https://pegs.org/event/whitney-stained-glass-studio-presentation-of-color-and-skill/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://pegs.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Pegs-Gallery-Event-FB-cover-photo-Whitney-Stained-Glass-Studeio.png
END:VEVENT
